    'Classic server-side vulnerabilities, such as SQL injection' => 'Kerentanan sisi server klasik, seperti SQL injection',
    'How do HTTP Host header vulnerabilities arise?' => 'Bagaimana kerentanan HTTP Host header muncul?',
    'HTTP Host header vulnerabilities typically arise due to the flawed assumption that the header is not user controllable. This creates implicit trust in the Host header and results in inadequate validation or escaping of its value, even though an attacker can easily modify this using tools like Burp Proxy.' => 'Kerentanan ini muncul akibat anggapan keliru bahwa Host header tidak dapat dimodifikasi pengguna, padahal penyerang dapat mengubahnya dengan mudah memakai proxy pencegat.',
    'Even if the Host header itself is handled more securely, depending on the configuration of the servers that deal with incoming requests, the Host can potentially be overridden by injecting other headers. Sometimes website owners are unaware that these headers are supported by default and, as a result, they may not be treated with the same level of scrutiny.' => 'Meski Host header utama sudah divalidasi, nilainya terkadang masih dapat ditimpa melalui header tambahan yang aktif secara bawaan tanpa disadari pengelola situs.',
    'In fact, many of these vulnerabilities arise not because of insecure coding but because of insecure configuration of one or more components in the related infrastructure. These configuration issues can occur because websites integrate third-party technologies into their architecture without necessarily understanding the configuration options and their security implications.' => 'Banyak celah Host header bersumber bukan dari bug kode semata, melainkan dari konfigurasi komponen infrastruktur pihak ketiga yang kurang dipahami implikasi keamanannya.',
    'Exploiting HTTP Host header vulnerabilities' => 'Mengeksploitasi kerentanan HTTP Host header',
    "By now, you should have a good understanding of what the HTTP Host header is. For pentesters and bug bounty hunters, we've created some additional guidance on how you can identify and exploit these kinds of vulnerabilities for yourself. We've also provided some deliberately vulnerable [[S0]]LABS[[/S0]] so that you can practice some of these techniques." => 'Setelah memahami cara kerja Host header, bagian lanjutan membahas teknik identifikasi serta eksploitasinya lengkap dengan [[S0]]LAB PRAKTIK[[/S0]].',
    'How to prevent HTTP Host header attacks' => 'Cara mencegah serangan HTTP Host header',
    'To prevent HTTP Host header attacks, the simplest approach is to avoid using the Host header altogether in server-side code. Double-check whether each URL really needs to be absolute. You will often find that you can just use a relative URL instead. This simple change can help you prevent web cache poisoning vulnerabilities in particular.' => 'Langkah paling sederhana adalah menghindari pembacaan Host header dalam kode server dan memakai URL relatif alih-alih URL absolut sebisa mungkin.',
    'Other ways to prevent HTTP Host header attacks include:' => 'Langkah pencegahan lainnya meliputi:',
    'Protect absolute URLs' => 'Lindungi URL absolut',
    'When you have to use absolute URLs, you should require the current domain to be manually specified in a configuration file and refer to this value instead of the Host header. This approach would eliminate the threat of password reset poisoning, for example.' => 'Jika URL absolut wajib digunakan, baca nama domain dari berkas konfigurasi statis, bukan dari Host header permintaan.',
    'Validate the Host header' => 'Validasi Host header',
    'If you must use the Host header, make sure you validate it properly. This should involve checking it against a whitelist of permitted domains and rejecting or redirecting any requests for unrecognized hosts. You should consult the documentation of your framework for guidance on how to do this. For example, the Django framework provides the [[C0]] option in the settings file. This approach will reduce your exposure to Host header injection attacks.' => 'Apabila Host header tetap diperlukan, cocokkan nilainya terhadap daftar domain yang diizinkan (whitelist) dan tolak host yang tidak dikenal, misalnya lewat opsi [[C0]] di Django.',
    "Don't support Host override headers" => 'Nonaktifkan header penimpa Host',
    'It is also important to check that you do not support additional headers that may be used to construct these attacks, in particular [[C0]]. Remember that these may be supported by default.' => 'Pastikan server tidak menerima header penimpa Host yang tidak diperlukan seperti [[C0]], karena sering aktif secara bawaan.',
    'Whitelist permitted domains' => 'Gunakan whitelist domain pada perantara',
    'To prevent routing-based attacks on internal infrastructure, you should configure your load balancer or any reverse proxies to forward requests only to a whitelist of permitted domains.' => 'Konfigurasikan load balancer dan reverse proxy agar hanya meneruskan permintaan menuju daftar domain yang diizinkan.',
    'Be careful with internal-only virtual hosts' => 'Pisahkan virtual host internal',
    'When using virtual hosting, you should avoid hosting internal-only websites and applications on the same server as public-facing content. Otherwise, attackers may be able to access internal domains via Host header manipulation.' => 'Hindari menaruh aplikasi internal satu server dengan situs publik agar penyerang tidak dapat mengakses sistem internal melalui manipulasi Host header.',

    // Exploiting page
    "In this section, we'll look more closely at how you can identify whether a website is vulnerable to HTTP Host header attacks. We'll then provide examples of how you can exploit this, along with several interactive labs that you can use to practice these exploits on a deliberately vulnerable website." => 'Bagian ini membahas langkah menguji kerentanan HTTP Host header beserta contoh skenario eksploitasi dan lab praktiknya.',
    'How to test for vulnerabilities using the HTTP Host header' => 'Cara menguji kerentanan melalui HTTP Host header',
    'To test whether a website is vulnerable to attack via the HTTP Host header, you will need an intercepting proxy, such as Burp Proxy, and manual testing tools like Burp Repeater and Burp Intruder.' => 'Untuk menguji kerentanan ini, Anda memerlukan proxy pencegat dan alat pengujian permintaan HTTP manual seperti Repeater maupun Intruder.',
    'In short, you need to identify whether you are able to modify the Host header and still reach the target application with your request. If so, you can use this header to probe the application and observe what effect this has on the response.' => 'Intinya, periksa apakah aplikasi target masih dapat dicapai setelah nilai Host header diubah. Jika ya, amati bagaimana aplikasi memproses nilai tersebut dalam respons.',
    'Supply an arbitrary Host header' => 'Kirimkan Host header sembarang',
    'When probing for Host header injection vulnerabilities, the first step is to test what happens when you supply an arbitrary, unrecognized domain name via the Host header.' => 'Langkah pertama adalah mengganti Host header dengan nama domain acak yang tidak dikenal dan melihat respons server.',
    "Some intercepting proxies derive the target IP address from the Host header directly, which makes this kind of testing all but impossible; any changes you made to the header would just cause the request to be sent to a completely different IP address. However, Burp Suite accurately maintains the separation between the Host header and the target IP address. This separation allows you to supply any arbitrary or malformed Host header that you want, while still making sure that the request is sent to the intended target." => 'Beberapa proxy menentukan alamat IP tujuan dari Host header, sehingga pengujian ini gagal karena paket terkirim ke server lain. Burp Suite memisahkan target koneksi dari nilai header sehingga Host header bebas dimodifikasi.',
    'The target URL is displayed either at the top of the panel (for Burp Repeater and Proxy interception) or on the "Target" tab in Burp Intruder. You can edit the target manually by clicking the pencil icon.' => 'URL target ditampilkan di bagian atas panel atau tab Target dan dapat diubah manual melalui ikon pensil.',
    "Sometimes, you will still be able to access the target website even when you supply an unexpected Host header. This could be for a number of reasons. For example, servers are sometimes configured with a default or fallback option in case they receive requests for domain names that they don't recognize. If your target website happens to be the default, you're in luck. In this case, you can begin studying what the application does with the Host header and whether this behavior is exploitable." => 'Jika situs tetap merespons dengan normal, biasanya target dikonfigurasi sebagai virtual host bawaan (fallback). Pada kondisi ini Anda bisa langsung meneliti pemanfaatan nilai Host oleh aplikasi.',
    'On the other hand, as the Host header is such a fundamental part of how the websites work, tampering with it often means you will be unable to reach the target application at all. The front-end server or load balancer that received your request may simply not know where to forward it, resulting in an "[[C0]]" error of some kind. This is especially likely if your target is accessed via a CDN. In this case, you should move on to trying some of the techniques outlined below.' => 'Sebaliknya, jika perantara atau CDN tidak mengenali Host baru dan membalas error seperti "[[C0]]", lanjutkan ke teknik pengujian lanjutan di bawah.',
    'Check for flawed validation' => 'Periksa cacat validasi',
    "Instead of receiving an \"[[C0]]\" response, you might find that your request is blocked as a result of some kind of security measure. For example, some websites will validate whether the Host header matches the SNI from the TLS handshake. This doesn't necessarily mean that they're immune to Host header attacks." => 'Terkadang permintaan ditolak mekanisme keamanan, seperti pencocokan Host header dengan SNI saat TLS handshake. Namun hal itu belum tentu menutup semua celah.',
    'You should try to understand how the website parses the Host header. This can sometimes reveal loopholes that can be used to bypass the validation. For example, some parsing algorithms will omit the port from the Host header, meaning that only the domain name is validated. If you are also able to supply a non-numeric port, you can leave the domain name untouched to ensure that you reach the target application, while potentially injecting a payload via the port.' => 'Amati cara aplikasi mem-parsing Host header. Sebagian parser membuang bagian port sebelum memvalidasi domain, sehingga Anda dapat menyelipkan payload di belakang tanda titik dua sebagai port non-numerik sambil mempertahankan nama domain asli.',
    'Other sites will try to apply matching logic to allow for arbitrary subdomains. In this case, you may be able to bypass the validation entirely by registering an arbitrary domain name that ends with the same sequence of characters as a whitelisted one:' => 'Situs lain mengizinkan pencocokan akhiran domain untuk menerima semua subdomain, yang bisa dilewati dengan mendaftarkan domain lain berakhiran karakter serupa:',
    'Alternatively, you could take advantage of a less-secure subdomain that you have already compromised:' => 'Atau manfaatkan subdomain lain yang lebih rentan dan sudah berhasil diambil alih:',
    'For further examples of common domain-validation flaws, check out our content on [[A0]]circumventing common SSRF defences[[/A0]] and [[A1]]Origin header parsing errors[[/A1]].' => 'Untuk contoh kesalahan validasi domain lainnya, pelajari materi [[A0]]melewati pertahanan SSRF umum[[/A0]] serta [[A1]]kesalahan parsing Origin header[[/A1]].',
    'Send ambiguous requests' => 'Kirim permintaan ambigu',
    'The code that validates the host and the code that does something vulnerable with it often reside in different application components or even on separate servers. By identifying and exploiting discrepancies in how they retrieve the Host header, you may be able to issue an ambiguous request that appears to have a different host depending on which system is looking at it.' => 'Kode yang memvalidasi Host sering berada di server berbeda dengan kode yang memakainya. Perbedaan cara membaca header di antara kedua sistem dapat dieksploitasi lewat permintaan ambigu.',
    'The following are just a few examples of how you may be able to create ambiguous requests.' => 'Berikut beberapa contoh cara menyusun permintaan ambigu.',
    'Inject duplicate Host headers' => 'Suntikkan Host header ganda',
    'One possible approach is to try adding duplicate Host headers. Admittedly, this will often just result in your request being blocked. However, as a browser is unlikely to ever send such a request, you may occasionally find that developers have not anticipated this scenario. In this case, you might expose some interesting behavioral quirks.' => 'Coba sertakan dua Host header sekaligus dalam satu permintaan. Walau sering ditolak, beberapa arsitektur tidak mengantisipasi kasus ini karena peramban normal tidak pernah melakukannya.',
    'Different systems and technologies will handle this case differently, but it is common for one of the two headers to be given precedence over the other one, effectively overriding its value. When systems disagree about which header is the correct one, this can lead to discrepancies that you may be able to exploit. Consider the following request:' => 'Jika dua komponen berbeda pendapat mengenai header mana yang dipakai (yang pertama atau yang terakhir), timbul ketidaksesuaian yang dapat dimanfaatkan:',
    "Let's say the front-end gives precedence to the first instance of the header, but the back-end prefers the final instance. Given this scenario, you could use the first header to ensure that your request is routed to the intended target and use the second header to pass your payload into the server-side code." => 'Apabila frontend memprioritaskan Host pertama untuk routing sementara backend membaca Host terakhir, payload pada header kedua tetap diproses kode backend.',
    'Supply an absolute URL' => 'Sertakan URL absolut di baris permintaan',
    'Although the request line typically specifies a relative path on the requested domain, many servers are also configured to understand requests for absolute URLs.' => 'Meskipun baris permintaan HTTP lazimnya berisi path relatif, banyak server menerima URL absolut.',
    "The ambiguity caused by supplying both an absolute URL and a Host header can also lead to discrepancies between different systems. Officially, the request line should be given precedence when routing the request but, in practice, this isn't always the case. You can potentially exploit these discrepancies in much the same way as duplicate Host headers." => 'Menyertakan URL absolut pada baris permintaan bersamaan dengan Host header berbeda dapat memicu perbedaan interpretasi antarserver perantara dan backend.',
    'Note that you may also need to experiment with different protocols. Servers will sometimes behave differently depending on whether the request line contains an HTTP or an HTTPS URL.' => 'Uji pula perbedaan protokol HTTP maupun HTTPS pada URL absolut tersebut karena respons server sering kali berbeda.',
    'Add line wrapping' => 'Tambahkan indentasi baris header',
    'You can also uncover quirky behavior by indenting HTTP headers with a space character. Some servers will interpret the indented header as a wrapped line and, therefore, treat it as part of the preceding header\'s value. Other servers will ignore the indented header altogether.' => 'Menambahkan spasi di awal baris header dapat diartikan sebagai sambungan header sebelumnya oleh sebagian server, sementara server lain mengabaikannya.',
    'Due to the highly inconsistent handling of this case, there will often be discrepancies between different systems that process your request. For example, consider the following request:' => 'Perbedaan penanganan baris terindentasi antarkomponen bisa membuka celah bypass validasi seperti contoh berikut:',
    'The website may block requests with multiple Host headers, but you may be able to bypass this validation by indenting one of them like this. If the front-end ignores the indented header, the request will be processed as an ordinary request for [[C0]]. Now let\'s say the back-end ignores the leading space and gives precedence to the first header in the case of duplicates. This discrepancy might allow you to pass arbitrary values via the "wrapped" Host header.' => 'Jika frontend mengabaikan baris berspasi dan meneruskan permintaan untuk [[C0]], sedangkan backend menganggap spasi awal tidak ada lalu memakai nilai header pertama, payload Anda berhasil lolos.',
    'Other techniques' => 'Teknik lainnya',
    "This is just a small sample of the many possible ways to issue harmful, ambiguous requests. For example, you can also adapt many HTTP request smuggling techniques to construct Host header attacks. We'll cover this in more detail in our dedicated request smuggling topic." => 'Berbagai teknik HTTP request smuggling juga dapat diadaptasi untuk menyusun serangan Host header.',
    '[[A0]]HTTP request smuggling.[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]HTTP request smuggling.[[/A0]]',
    'Inject host override headers' => 'Suntikkan header penimpa Host',
    "Even if you can't override the Host header using an ambiguous request, there are other possibilities for overriding its value while leaving it intact. This includes injecting your payload via one of several other HTTP headers that are designed to serve just this purpose, albeit for more innocent use cases." => 'Jika Host header asli tidak bisa dimodifikasi, periksa apakah aplikasi mendukung header alternatif yang memang dirancang untuk menyampaikan nama host asli pengguna.',
    "As we've already discussed, websites are often accessed via some kind of intermediary system, such as a load balancer or a reverse proxy. In this kind of architecture, the Host header that the back-end server receives may contain the domain name for one of these intermediary systems. This is usually not relevant for the requested functionality." => 'Dalam arsitektur reverse proxy atau load balancer, Host header yang diterima backend terkadang sudah diganti menjadi nama host internal perantara.',
    "To solve this problem, the front-end may inject the [[C0]] header, containing the original value of the Host header from the client's initial request. For this reason, when an[[C1]] header is present, many frameworks will refer to this instead. You may observe this behavior even when there is no front-end that uses this header." => 'Untuk mengatasinya, perantara menyisipkan header [[C0]] berisi nilai Host awal dari klien. Banyak framework otomatis membaca header[[C1]] saat header tersebut dikirim dalam permintaan.',
    'You can sometimes use [[C0]] to inject your malicious input while circumventing any validation on the Host header itself.' => 'Dengan menyisipkan [[C0]], Anda kerap dapat menimpa domain yang dipakai aplikasi sambil menjaga Host header asli tetap valid.',
    'Although [[C0]] is the de facto standard for this behavior, you may come across other headers that serve a similar purpose, including:' => 'Selain [[C0]] sebagai standar paling umum, beberapa header alternatif yang berfungsi serupa antara lain:',
    'In Burp Suite, you can use the [[A0]]Param Miner[[/A0]] extension\'s "Guess headers" function to automatically probe for supported headers using its extensive built-in wordlist.' => 'Anda dapat memakai fitur "Guess headers" pada ekstensi [[A0]]Param Miner[[/A0]] untuk mendeteksi header penimpa yang didukung secara otomatis.',
    'From a security perspective, it is important to note that some websites, potentially even your own, support this kind of behavior unintentionally. This is usually because one or more of these headers is enabled by default in some third-party technology that they use.' => 'Banyak situs mendukung header penimpa ini tanpa disadari karena diaktifkan secara bawaan oleh framework atau web server pihak ketiga.',
    'How to exploit the HTTP Host header' => 'Cara mengeksploitasi HTTP Host header',
    'Once you have identified that you can pass arbitrary hostnames to the target application, you can start to look for ways to exploit it.' => 'Begitu Anda memastikan nama host sembarang dapat diteruskan ke aplikasi, tahap selanjutnya adalah mencari skenario eksploitasinya.',
    "In this section, we'll provide some examples of common HTTP Host header attacks that you may be able to construct. We've also created some deliberately vulnerable websites so that you can see how these exploits work and put what you've learned to the test." => 'Berikut beberapa serangan umum berbasis Host header beserta lab praktiknya.',
    "We'll cover the following examples:" => 'Contoh skenario yang dibahas mencakup:',
    '[[A0]]Password reset poisoning[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Password reset poisoning[[/A0]]',
    'Attackers can sometimes use the Host header for password reset poisoning attacks.' => 'Penyerang dapat memanfaatkan Host header untuk meracuni tautan atur ulang kata sandi.',
    'Web cache poisoning via the Host header' => 'Web cache poisoning melalui Host header',
    "When probing for potential Host header attacks, you will often come across seemingly vulnerable behavior that isn't directly exploitable. For example, you may find that the Host header is reflected in the response markup without HTML-encoding, or even used directly in script imports. Reflected, client-side vulnerabilities, such as XSS, are typically not exploitable when they're caused by the Host header. There is no way for an attacker to force a victim's browser to issue an incorrect host in a useful manner." => 'Nilai Host header kerap memantul di respons HTML atau URL skrip tanpa encoding. Karena penyerang tidak bisa memaksa peramban korban mengirim Host palsu secara langsung, celah pantulan ini biasanya tidak langsung terpakai.',
    'However, if the target uses a web cache, it may be possible to turn this useless, reflected vulnerability into a dangerous, stored one by persuading the cache to serve a poisoned response to other users.' => 'Namun jika situs memakai web cache, respons beracun hasil manipulasi Host dapat tersimpan di cache lalu dikirim ke pengguna lain.',
    "To construct a web cache poisoning attack, you need to elicit a response from the server that reflects an injected payload. The challenge is to do this while preserving a cache key that will still be mapped to other users' requests. If successful, the next step is to get this malicious response cached. It will then be served to any users who attempt to visit the affected page." => 'Caranya adalah memicu respons yang memantulkan payload tanpa mengubah cache key permintaan, sehingga respons beracun tersimpan dan disajikan ke pengunjung berikutnya.',
    'Standalone caches typically include the Host header in the cache key, so this approach usually works best on integrated, application-level caches. That said, the techniques discussed earlier can sometimes enable you to poison even standalone web caches.' => 'Cache terpisah umumnya memasukkan Host header ke cache key, namun header penimpa atau cacat parsing tetap dapat meracuni cache tingkat aplikasi maupun cache terpisah.',
    'Web cache poisoning is covered extensively in a dedicated topic on the Web Security Academy.' => 'Pembahasan lengkap web cache poisoning tersedia pada topik khususnya.',
    'Web cache poisoning' => 'Web cache poisoning',
    'Exploiting classic server-side vulnerabilities' => 'Mengeksploitasi kerentanan sisi server klasik',
    'Every HTTP header is a potential vector for exploiting classic server-side vulnerabilities, and the Host header is no exception. For example, you should try the usual SQL injection probing techniques via the Host header. If the value of the header is passed into a SQL statement, this could be exploitable.' => 'Sebagaimana header HTTP lainnya, Host header dapat menjadi titik masuk celah sisi server klasik seperti SQL injection apabila nilainya diteruskan ke kueri basis data.',
    'Accessing restricted functionality' => 'Mengakses fungsionalitas terbatas',
    "For fairly obvious reasons, it is common for websites to restrict access to certain functionality to internal users only. However, some websites' access control features make flawed assumptions that allow you to bypass these restrictions by making simple modifications to the Host header. This can expose an increased attack surface for other exploits." => 'Banyak situs membatasi fitur tertentu khusus untuk pengguna internal hanya dengan memeriksa Host header permintaan, sehingga kontrol tersebut mudah dilewati.',
    'Accessing internal websites with virtual host brute-forcing' => 'Mengakses situs internal melalui brute-force virtual host',
    "Companies sometimes make the mistake of hosting publicly accessible websites and private, internal sites on the same server. Servers typically have both a public and a private IP address. As the internal hostname may resolve to the private IP address, this scenario can't always be detected simply by looking at DNS records:" => 'Perusahaan terkadang menempatkan situs publik dan situs internal di satu server fisik yang sama. Karena nama host internal hanya terpetakan ke IP privat, keberadaannya tidak selalu tampak di DNS publik:',
    'In some cases, the internal site might not even have a public DNS record associated with it. Nonetheless, an attacker can typically access any virtual host on any server that they have access to, provided they can guess the hostnames. If they have discovered a hidden domain name through other means, such as information disclosure, they could simply request this directly. Otherwise, they can use tools like Burp Intruder to brute-force virtual hosts using a simple wordlist of candidate subdomains.' => 'Selama penyerang bisa menebak nama host internal (baik lewat kebocoran informasi maupun brute-force subdomain pada Host header), situs internal tersebut dapat diakses langsung.',
    'It is sometimes also possible to use the Host header to launch high-impact, routing-based SSRF attacks. These are sometimes known as "Host header SSRF attacks", and were explored in depth by SecDevLab Research in [[A0]]Cracking the lens: targeting HTTP\'s hidden attack-surface[[/A0]].' => 'Host header juga dapat dipakai untuk melancarkan SSRF berbasis routing, yang dibahas secara mendalam pada riset [[A0]]Cracking the lens: targeting HTTP\'s hidden attack-surface[[/A0]].',
    'Classic SSRF vulnerabilities are usually based on XXE or exploitable business logic that sends HTTP requests to a URL derived from user-controllable input. Routing-based SSRF, on the other hand, relies on exploiting the intermediary components that are prevalent in many cloud-based architectures. This includes in-house load balancers and reverse proxies.' => 'Berbeda dari SSRF biasa yang menyalahgunakan parameter URL aplikasi, SSRF berbasis routing menargetkan load balancer atau reverse proxy dalam arsitektur cloud.',
    'Although these components are deployed for different purposes, fundamentally, they receive requests and forward them to the appropriate back-end. If they are insecurely configured to forward requests based on an unvalidated Host header, they can be manipulated into misrouting requests to an arbitrary system of the attacker\'s choice.' => 'Jika komponen perantara dikonfigurasi untuk meneruskan lalu lintas berdasarkan Host header tanpa validasi, penyerang dapat membelokkan permintaan menuju host lain sesuka hati.',
    'These systems make fantastic targets. They sit in a privileged network position that allows them to receive requests directly from the public web, while also having access to much, if not all, of the internal network. This makes the Host header a powerful vector for SSRF attacks, potentially transforming a simple load balancer into a gateway to the entire internal network.' => 'Karena berada di perbatasan jaringan publik dan privat, load balancer yang rentan dapat berubah menjadi gerbang menuju seluruh jaringan internal.',
    'You can use Burp Collaborator to help identify these vulnerabilities. If you supply the domain of your Collaborator server in the Host header, and subsequently receive a DNS lookup from the target server or another in-path system, this indicates that you may be able to route requests to arbitrary domains.' => 'Penguji dapat memasukkan domain server pemantau eksternal ke Host header; datangnya kueri DNS menandakan permintaan diteruskan keluar.',
    "Having confirmed that you can successfully manipulate an intermediary system to route your requests to an arbitrary public server, the next step is to see if you can exploit this behavior to access internal-only systems. To do this, you'll need to identify private IP addresses that are in use on the target's internal network. In addition to any IP addresses that are leaked by the application, you can also scan hostnames belonging to the company to see if any resolve to a private IP address. If all else fails, you can still identify valid IP addresses by simply brute-forcing standard private IP ranges, such as [[C0]]." => 'Setelah memastikan perantara mau meneruskan permintaan ke host luar, langkah selanjutnya adalah memindai alamat IP privat pada jaringan internal seperti rentang [[C0]].',
    'IP address ranges are commonly expressed using CIDR notation, for example, [[C0]].' => 'Rentang alamat IP umumnya ditulis dengan notasi CIDR, misalnya [[C0]].',
    'IPv4 addresses consist of four 8-bit decimal values known as "octets", each separated by a dot. The value of each octet can range from 0 to 255, meaning that the lowest possible IPv4 address would be [[C0]] and the highest [[C1]].' => 'Alamat IPv4 terdiri atas empat oktet desimal 8-bit bernilai 0 hingga 255, mulai dari [[C0]] sampai [[C1]].',
    'In CIDR notation, the lowest IP address in the range is written explicitly, followed by another number that indicates how many bits from the start of the given address are fixed for the entire range. For example, [[C0]] indicates that the first 8 bits are fixed (the first octet). In other words, this range includes all IP addresses from [[C1]] to [[C2]].' => 'Notasi CIDR menuliskan IP awal diikuti jumlah bit awalan yang tetap; contohnya [[C0]] mencakup seluruh alamat dari [[C1]] hingga [[C2]].',
    'Connection state attacks' => 'Serangan status koneksi',
    "For performance reasons, many websites reuse connections for multiple request/response cycles with the same client. Poorly implemented HTTP servers sometimes work on the dangerous assumption that certain properties, such as the Host header, are identical for all HTTP/1.1 requests sent over the same connection. This may be true of requests sent by a browser, but isn't necessarily the case for a sequence of requests sent from Burp Repeater. This can lead to a number of potential issues." => 'Untuk efisiensi performa, server kerap memakai ulang koneksi HTTP/1.1 untuk beberapa permintaan sekaligus, lalu keliru berasumsi bahwa Host header tiap permintaan pada koneksi itu selalu sama.',
    'For example, you may occasionally encounter servers that only perform thorough validation on the first request they receive over a new connection. In this case, you can potentially bypass this validation by sending an innocent-looking initial request then following up with your malicious one down the same connection.' => 'Jika validasi penuh hanya dilakukan pada permintaan pertama saat koneksi baru dibuka, penyerang dapat mengirim permintaan normal terlebih dahulu lalu menyusulkan permintaan berbahaya di koneksi yang sama.',
    'Many reverse proxies use the Host header to route requests to the correct back-end. If they assume that all requests on the connection are intended for the same host as the initial request, this can provide a useful vector for a number of Host header attacks, including routing-based SSRF, password reset poisoning, and cache poisoning.' => 'Selain itu, reverse proxy yang menjaga keputusan routing dari permintaan pertama di koneksi yang sama juga dapat dieksploitasi untuk SSRF, password reset poisoning, dan cache poisoning.',
    'SSRF via a malformed request line' => 'SSRF melalui baris permintaan cacat',
    'Custom proxies sometimes fail to validate the request line properly, which can allow you to supply unusual, malformed input with unfortunate results.' => 'Proxy kustom terkadang gagal memvalidasi format baris permintaan HTTP sehingga rentan terhadap path tak wajar.',
    'For example, a reverse proxy might take the path from the request line, prefix it with [[C0]], and route the request to that upstream URL. This works fine if the path starts with a [[C1]] character, but what if starts with an [[C2]] character instead?' => 'Misalnya, proxy menggabungkan [[C0]] dengan path dari baris permintaan. Jika path diawali [[C2]] alih-alih [[C1]], parser URL dapat salah mengartikan tujuan hostnya:',
    'The resulting upstream URL will be [[C0]], which most HTTP libraries interpret as a request to access [[C1]] with the username [[C2]].' => 'URL tujuan menjadi [[C0]], yang ditafsirkan pustaka HTTP sebagai permintaan menuju [[C1]] memakai kredensial pengguna [[C2]].',
    'These techniques were also popularized by our Director of Research, James Kettle. For a more detailed description of the technique, tooling, and how he was able to exploit these vulnerabilities in the wild, check out the full whitepaper and video presentation on our Research page.' => 'Teknik-teknik ini turut dipopulerkan oleh Direktur Riset James Kettle melalui makalah dan presentasi riset resminya.',
    "[[A0]]Cracking the lens: targeting HTTP's hidden attack-surface[[/A0]]" => '[[A0]]Cracking the lens: targeting HTTP\'s hidden attack-surface[[/A0]]',
    '[[A0]]SecDevLab research[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Riset SecDevLab[[/A0]]',

    // Password reset poisoning page
    'Password reset poisoning is a technique whereby an attacker manipulates a vulnerable website into generating a password reset link pointing to a domain under their control. This behavior can be leveraged to steal the secret tokens required to reset arbitrary users\' passwords and, ultimately, compromise their accounts.' => 'Password reset poisoning adalah teknik memanipulasi situs agar menghasilkan tautan pengaturan ulang kata sandi yang mengarah ke domain milik penyerang, guna mencuri token rahasia dan mengambil alih akun korban.',
    '[[A0]]This technique was first documented in 2013 by our Director of Research, James Kettle.[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Teknik ini pertama kali didokumentasikan pada tahun 2013 oleh Direktur Riset James Kettle.[[/A0]]',
    '[[A0]]Check out our Research page for full write-ups and video presentations of more innovative techniques discovered by James and the rest of the team.[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Kunjungi halaman riset untuk membaca makalah lengkap teknik temuan tim peneliti lainnya.[[/A0]]',
    'How does a password reset work?' => 'Bagaimana cara kerja fitur atur ulang kata sandi?',
    'Virtually all websites that require a login also implement functionality that allows users to reset their password if they forget it. There are several ways of doing this, with varying degrees of security and practicality. One of the most common approaches goes something like this:' => 'Hampir semua situs dengan sistem login menyediakan fitur lupa kata sandi. Alur yang paling sering dijumpai berjalan sebagai berikut:',
    'The user enters their username or email address and submits a password reset request.' => 'Pengguna memasukkan username atau alamat email lalu mengajukan permintaan atur ulang kata sandi.',
    "The website checks that this user exists and then generates a temporary, unique, high-entropy token, which it associates with the user's account on the back-end." => 'Server memverifikasi keberadaan akun lalu membuat token acak sementara yang terikat pada akun tersebut.',
    'The website sends an email to the user that contains a link for resetting their password. The user\'s unique reset token is included as a query parameter in the corresponding URL:' => 'Situs mengirim email berisi tautan atur ulang kata sandi dengan token unik pada parameter kueri URL:',
    'When the user visits this URL, the website checks whether the provided token is valid and uses it to determine which account is being reset. If everything is as expected, the user is given the option to enter a new password. Finally, the token is destroyed.' => 'Saat pengguna membuka tautan itu, server memvalidasi token, mengizinkan penggantian kata sandi baru, lalu menghapus token agar tidak dipakai ulang.',
    'This process is simple enough and relatively secure in comparison to some other approaches. However, its security relies on the principle that only the intended user has access to their email inbox and, therefore, to their unique token. Password reset poisoning is a method of stealing this token in order to change another user\'s password.' => 'Keamanan alur ini bertumpu pada asumsi bahwa hanya pemilik akun yang bisa membaca kotak masuk email dan melihat token tersebut. Password reset poisoning mematahkan asumsi itu dengan mencuri tokennya.',
    'How to construct a password reset poisoning attack' => 'Cara menyusun serangan password reset poisoning',
    'If the URL that is sent to the user is dynamically generated based on controllable input, such as the Host header, it may be possible to construct a password reset poisoning attack as follows:' => 'Apabila domain tautan di email dibuat secara dinamis dari masukan yang dapat dikendalikan seperti Host header, penyerang dapat melakukannya lewat langkah berikut:',
    "The attacker obtains the victim's email address or username, as required, and submits a password reset request on their behalf. When submitting the form, they intercept the resulting HTTP request and modify the Host header so that it points to a domain that they control. For this example, we'll use [[C0]]." => 'Penyerang mengajukan permintaan atur ulang kata sandi memakai email atau username korban, lalu mencegat permintaan HTTP-nya dan mengganti Host header menjadi domain kendali sendiri seperti [[C0]].',
    'The victim receives a genuine password reset email directly from the website. This seems to contain an ordinary link to reset their password and, crucially, contains a valid password reset token that is associated with their account. However, the domain name in the URL points to the attacker\'s server:' => 'Korban menerima email resmi dari situs, namun domain di dalam tautan atur ulang kata sandi bersama token validnya kini mengarah ke server penyerang:',
    'If the victim clicks this link (or it is fetched in some other way, for example, by an antivirus scanner) the password reset token will be delivered to the attacker\'s server.' => 'Jika korban mengklik tautan tersebut (atau dipindai otomatis oleh pemindai tautan email), token rahasia langsung terkirim ke log server penyerang.',
    "The attacker can now visit the real URL for the vulnerable website and supply the victim's stolen token via the corresponding parameter. They will then be able to reset the user's password to whatever they like and subsequently log in to their account." => 'Penyerang tinggal membuka URL asli situs target sembari menyertakan token curian tadi untuk menetapkan kata sandi baru dan masuk ke akun korban.',
    'In a real attack, the attacker may seek to increase the probability of the victim clicking the link by first warming them up with a fake breach notification, for example.' => 'Dalam serangan nyata, penyerang sering menyertai aksi ini dengan rekayasa sosial agar korban terdorong mengeklik tautan email.',
    "Even if you can't control the password reset link, you can sometimes use the Host header to inject HTML into sensitive emails. Note that email clients typically don't execute JavaScript, but other HTML injection techniques like [[A0]]dangling markup attacks[[/A0]] may still apply." => 'Bahkan saat domain tautan tidak bisa diubah, Host header terkadang tetap memantul ke tubuh email sehingga membuka celah injeksi HTML atau [[A0]]serangan dangling markup[[/A0]].',
];
